/// PLACEHOLDER — overwritten at runtime by `hookkit_pkl_config::eval`.
///
/// `stage_builtins()` generates a fresh `Builtins.pkl` aggregator in the
/// staging temp dir by scanning the embedded `tools/` directory. Every
/// `tools/<name>.pkl` becomes a top-level property keyed by camelCase of
/// the filename (`cargo_fmt.pkl` → `cargoFmt`).
///
/// That means adding a new builtin is a single-file change: drop a new
/// `tools/<name>.pkl` exporting a `spec: Config.ToolSpec`. No edits to this
/// file required — leave it as-is.
///
/// The body below is just a static snapshot for compile-time `include_dir!`
/// embedding; it gets clobbered the moment a config is evaluated.

module agent_hook_kit.PostToolUseBuiltins

import "Config.pkl" as Config

// Snapshot of the catalog as of the most recent foundation commit. The
// runtime regenerates this from `tools/` and ignores whatever is here.
